DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmiiddiiccaatt utility receives MIDI data from the given input MIDI port
     and/or sends it to the given output MIDI port.  The options are as fol‐
     lows:

     --dd      Dump transferred data in hex on stderr.

     --ii _f_i_l_e
             Read MIDI data from this file instead of receiving it from the
             MIDI port.  If the option argument is ‘-’ then standard input
             will be used.

     --oo _f_i_l_e
             Write MIDI data to this file instead of sending it to the MIDI
             port.  If the option argument is ‘-’ then standard output will be
             used.

     --qq _p_o_r_t
             Use this sndio(7) MIDI port for input/output.  If the option is
             used twice, the first one specifies the input port and the second
             one the output port.

     If no files are specified, then mmiiddiiccaatt transfers data from the MIDI in‐
     put port to the MIDI output port.

